      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Sarum missal, 13th century; Common of one Virgin Martyr, f. 205r. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of Gallica's image of f. 205r (October 2026), written as square notation on the manuscript's four lines with its C clefs.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
